    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added the disposable-email blocklist rule as a new, self-contained validation unit rather than modifying any existing method \u2014 keeping structural impact at essentially zero (no existing function changed; one new file).\n\n**New file:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice.java`\n\nIt follows the repo's existing `@ControllerAdvice` + `Validator` pattern (same as `OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`), which is exactly how other field-level owner rules produce a 400. It:\n\n- Extracts the domain after the last `@`, compared case-insensitively against the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- Rejects the `email` field via `errors.rejectValue(...)`, which surfaces as a `400 Bad Request` through the existing binding/exception advice.\n- Leaves owners with no email untouched.\n\nEvery method in the new class has cyclomatic complexity 1\u20132 and the class carries almost no surrounding complexity, so the `WMC_other * CC * changed_lines` cost stays minimal, and only one file is touched. The targeted test and the full suite are green.",
